    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0448" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/3–947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-09T17:00:00+08:00">March 9, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 9—5:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>500. Special representative Gimo departed Nanking this morning by air for Taipei.
                    (Reference Embassy’s telegram 499, March 9.) Colonel F. J. Dau, Assistant
                    Military Attaché, acting as Embassy courier, proceeded on same aircraft to
                    observe situation.</p>
                <p>Press currently reporting impending relief of General Chen Yi as Governor of
                    Taiwan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
